    <briefdescription>
<para>Reset of a caller&apos;s result object at the outermost public evaluation entry (C7). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Public functions that fill a <ref refid="structxThermal_1_1ThermodynamicProperties" kindref="compound">ThermodynamicProperties</ref> object create one of these first. If the call comes from outside the library (evaluation depth 0 on this thread), the object is reset to a default-constructed state, so no field of a previous call survives. Calls the library makes internally (H-P-X -&gt; T-P-X, brine -&gt; water backend) see a depth &gt; 0 and keep their intermediate state, so the result of a fresh evaluation is unchanged. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
